        {
          "#text": "coating; surface layer; protective layer",
          "@xml:lang": "en"
        },
        {
          "#text": "涂层；表面层；保护层",
          "@xml:lang": "zh"
        }
      ],
      "common:generalComment": [
        {
          "#text": "A coating is a covering that is applied to the surface of an object, usually referred to as the substrate. The purpose of applying the coating may be decorative, functional, or both. Coatings may be applied as liquids, gases or solids. Paints and lacquers are coatings that mostly have dual uses of protecting the substrate and being decorative. A protective coating is a layer of material that is applied to a substrate to prevent it from being damaged by environmental factors such as corrosion, abrasion and weathering.",
          "@xml:lang": "en"
        },
        {
          "#text": "涂层是涂在物体（通常称为基体）表面的覆盖物。涂覆的目的可以是装饰性的，也可以是功能性的，或者两者兼而有之。涂层可以是液体、气体或固体。油漆和涂料大多具有保护基材和装饰的双重用途。保护涂层是涂在基材上的一层材料，用于防止基材受到腐蚀、磨损和风化等环境因素的破坏。",
          "@xml:lang": "zh"
        }
      ],
